{"query":"Sen. Lindsey Graham said \"President Donald Trump probably knows more about medicine and specifically viruses than the so called scientists at the NIH and CDC\". evidence","results":[{"position":1,"site_name":"www.snopes.com","snippet":"# Did US Sen. Graham Say Trump Knows More Than CDC About Medicine?\n## The senator defended President Donald Trump's handling of the new coronavirus outbreak, but he didn't go this far.\n### Published March 2, 2020\n### Dan Evon\n\nClaim:\n\nU.S. Sen. Lindsey Graham said, \"President Trump probably knows more about medicine and specifically viruses than any of the so-called scientists at the NIH and CDC.\"\n\nRating:\n\nFalse\n\nFalse ### Published March 2, 2020\nOn Feb. 26, 2020, a quote ostensibly uttered by U.S. Sen. Lindsey Graham defending President Donald Trump's handling of an outbreak of new coronavirus was circulated on social media. Graham supposedly said: \"President Trump probably knows more about medicine and specifically viruses than any of the so-called scientists at the NIH and CDC. This is not a genuine quote from Graham.\n\nWe could not find the quote published by any credible publication. Our search of the senator's social media pages for this quote also turned up empty-handed. The above-displayed tweet appears to be the originating source for this quote. And since this account belongs to Dan Lyons, a writer who frequently shares jokes, sarcastic quips, and outright fabrications on his Twitter feed (Lyons was behind the viral Fake Steve Jobs account), it's safe to say that this quote was conjured out of thin air. Trump was criticized for his handling of the new coronavirus outbreak, with some saying that he downplayed the threat it posed to the United States. Trump, in turn, accused Democrats of \"politicizing\" the virus. While Graham did not say that Trump knew more about viruses than the CDC, he did defend the president's handling of the outbreak. Here's the statement Graham released on Feb. 26:\n\n> \"I appreciate President Trump's determination and leadership and his administration's efforts to contain the spread of the coronavirus and keep our country safe. > \"President Trump's decision to put Vice President Pence in charge of our nation's efforts to contain the coronavirus is an excellent idea and I have all the confidence in the world that the Vice President and his team will do everything in their power to contain this deadly virus. > \"This is a difficult situation for the world at large. We must be agile and aggressive in our approach to containing this virus. I'm confident the Trump administration, working with Congress, will do everything possible to keep the American people safe and healthy.\" #### Sources\nBekeimpis, Victoria, Martin Pengelly, and Golden, Hallie.   \"Trump Fends Off Criticism of 'Hoax' Remark After First US Coronavirus Death.\"     *The Guardian*.   29 February 2020. {\"reviewRating\":{\"alternateName\":\"False\"}}","title":"Did US Sen. Graham Say Trump Knows More Than CDC About Medicine?","url":"https://www.snopes.com/fact-check/lindsey-graham-trump-cdc/"},{"position":2,"site_name":"www.reuters.com","snippet":"# False claim: Sen. Lindsey Graham said Donald Trump probably knows more about medicine and viruses than any scientist at the NIH and CDC\nA viral tweet circulating on social media alleges that U.S. Senator Lindsey Graham said that President Donald Trump \"probably knows more about medicine and specifically viruses than any of the so-called scientists at the NIH and CDC. If anyone is going to eradicate this plague it'll be the president.\" The claim has at least 1,154 shares on Facebook (see examples  here and here;) and at least 615 Retweets on Twitter as of March 3,2020. The tweet in its entirety read: “CAPITOL HILL: @LindseyGrahamSC says @realDonaldTrump \"probably knows more about medicine and specifically viruses than any of the so-called scientists at the NIH and CDC. If anyone is going to eradicate this plague it'll be the president.\" It also included an authentic photo of Senator Graham (see photo here). This quote is false. The alleged statement was originally tweeted by Dan Lyons as satire (@RealDanLyons, see tweet archive.ph/0gHlD) on February 26, 2020. While it was intended as satire, it has been shared by users as an authentic quote from Graham (some examples of users answering to the tweet thinking it might be real can be seen here and here) and it was replicated by other users in their own tweets as if real (examples here and here;. “Lindsey Graham did not say that President Trump knows more about medicine and science than actual doctors and scientists. Nor did he say that President Trump was the only person who could stomp out the virus. This tweet was part of a string of tweets satirizing Trump enablers. I don't know why this one caught on except that apparently, it's just believable enough. I'm sorry that the joke fell flat”, Lyons told Reuters. After the incident, Lyon also publicly announced that he was deleting the rest of the satiric tweets in question and clarifying them.\n\nSenator Lindsey Graham did not say Trump knows more about medicine and viruses than any other scientist at the NIH and CDC. This claim surged from a satirical tweet from writer Dan Lyons and has already been publicly clarified by Lyons himself. False: Lindsey Graham did not say this; the claim originated from a satirical tweet by author Dan Lyons","title":"False claim: Sen. Lindsey Graham said Donald Trump probably knows more about medicine and viruses than any scientist at the NIH and CDC","url":"https://www.reuters.com/article/uk-factcheck-lindsey-graham-quote/false-claim-sen-lindsey-graham-said-donald-trump-probably-knows-more-about-medicine-and-viruses-than-any-scientist-at-the-nih-and-cdc-idUSKBN20R19W/"},{"position":3,"site_name":"politifact.com","snippet":"### Stand up for the facts!\n#### I would like to contribute\nFacebook posts stated on March 2, 2020 in a Facebook post:\n\nQuotes Sen. Lindsey Graham as saying President Trump “probably knows more about medicine and specifically viruses than any of the so-called scientists at the NIH and CDC.”\n\nPants on Fire goes to claims rated false and ridiculous. # Lindsey Graham quote on Trump knowing more about viruses than CDC is fake\n#### If your time is short\n- Sen. Lindsey Graham didn’t say that President Trump probably knows more about medicine and viruses than medical professionals.\n- The quote was fabricated by a Twitter account that has posted fake statements in the past.\n\nA popular tweet alleges that Republican Sen. Lindsey Graham suggested President Donald Trump “probably” knows more about medicine and viruses than the NIH and the CDC. The tweet, which has been deleted, is circulating on other social media platforms and reads:\n\n“CAPITOL HILL: @LindseyGrahamSC says @realDonaldTrump “probably knows more about medicine and specifically viruses than any of the so-called scientists at the NIH and CDC. If anyone is going to eradicate this plague it’ll be the president.” The post was flagged as part of Facebook’s efforts to combat false news and misinformation on its News Feed.\n\nThis is not a genuine quote by Graham. No credible news reports have published the statement, and we couldn’t find it on any of the senator’ s social media pages. Graham released a statement on Feb. 26 praising Trump’s response to the current coronavirus outbreak, but he doesn’t suggest in that statement that he believes Trump knows more about the virus than medical professionals. The person who tweeted the made-up quote, Dan Lyons, describes himself on his Twitter account as an “inventor of fake news.” But this context is lost on people who viewed the tweet on other platforms and those who didn’t visit his profile. ##### Our Sources\nFacebook post, March 2, 2020\n\nArchive.is, tweet, Feb. 26, 2020\n\nSenate.gov, Graham on Coronavirus Response, Feb. 26, 2020 Sen. Lindsey Graham, Twitter, Facebook, Accessed March 4, 2020\n\nReuters, False claim: Sen. Lindsey Graham said Donald Trump probably knows more about medicine and viruses than any scientist at the NIH and CDC, March 4, 2020 Snopes, Did US Sen. Graham Say Trump Knows More Than CDC About Medicine?, March 2, 2020 ## Lindsey Graham quote on Trump knowing more about viruses than CDC is fake\n“No,” she hasn’t taken money from utility companies for her U.S. Senate campaign.\n\nMostly False\n\nBy Caleb McCullough • July 29, 2026\n\nJames Fishback\n\nJames Fishback stated on July 23, 2026 in X post:\n\nThe U.S. Congress just “voted to merge our military with Israel’s military.”\n\nFalse","title":"Lindsey Graham quote on Trump knowing more about viruses than CDC is fake","url":"https://politifact.com/factchecks/2020/mar/05/facebook-posts/lindsey-graham-quote-trump-knowing-more-about-viru/"},{"position":4,"site_name":"www.newsweek.com","snippet":"The quote, which cites Graham saying that Trump will \"eradicate this plague,\" originated from a satire Twitter account. A viral quote attributed to Republican Senator Lindsey Graham is not real. The fake quote, which has Graham stating that President Donald Trump knows more about viruses than scientists, gained traction on Twitter last week. However, the quote was posted by satirical author Dan Lyons, whose Twitter bio reads, \"aka Fake Steve, inventor of fake news.\" \"CAPITOL HILL: @LindseyGrahamSC says @realDonaldTrump \"probably knows more about medicine and specifically viruses than any of the so-called scientists at the NIH [National Institute of Health] and CDC [Centers for Disease Control]. If anyone is going to eradicate this plague it'll be the president,\" Lyons wrote. On Sunday, historian and author Kevin Kruse retweeted the quote, informing people that it is not real. \"This is fake. Stop retweeting this account please,\" Kruse wrote as a reply to Lyon's tweet. Newsweek was unable to find any evidence of Graham saying this. The fact-checking site, Snopes, also came up empty in their investigation.  \"I appreciate President Trump's determination and leadership and his administration's efforts to contain the spread of the coronavirus and keep our country safe,\" Graham said in a statement posted to his website. Though the quote was posted by an account known for its satirical content, this is not the first time a prominent political figure has been falsely accused of saying something detrimental. Individuals making between $9,525 – $38,700 would be taxed at the current rate of 12 percent under his tax plan. The post about Sanders' tax plan was flagged by Facebook in an effort to stop the spread of fake news and misinformation. In October 2019, Trump was also the subject of a fake quote that went viral. At the time, he was accused of referring to the President of Italy, Sergio Mattarella, as \"President Mozzarella.\" The claims began after a press conference was held between Trump and Mattarella. After the press conference, many claimed Trump mispronounced Mattarella's name and instead said \"President Mozzarella,\" but according to Snopes, there was no evidence showing this mispronunciation. In June 2018, former President Barack Obama was also falsely accused of making comments about Trump. \"If we don't do something about this president, I will,\" Obama was cited to have said while speaking at a Democratic National Committee fundraiser. The quote gained traction across social media, but was determined to be false by Snopes. # That Viral Lindsey Graham Quote Saying Trump Knows More About Viruses Than Scientists Is Fake\n#### Read More on News\nIf anyone is going to eradicate this plague it'll be the president,\" Lyons wrote. \"This is fake. Stop retweeting this account please,\" Kruse wrote as a reply to Lyon's tweet. Parker Molloy, editor at large for Media Matters, also chimed in on the false claim, writing, \"the replies to Kevin's tweet, pointing out that the quote (which a lot of people seem to be sharing as if it were real) is fake, and depressing.\" *Newsweek* was unable to find any evidence of Graham saying this. The fact-checking site, Snopes, also came up empty in their investigation.\n\nHowever, Graham released a statement on February 26, discussing Trump's response to the coronavirus, which has infected over 89,000 people in at least 61 countries and killed over 3,000, according to Johns Hopkins University. \"I appreciate President Trump's determination and leadership and his administration's efforts to contain the spread of the coronavirus and keep our country safe,\" Graham said in a statement posted to his website.\n\nGraham's office did not respond to *Newsweek*'s request for comment for this story by publication time. In October 2019, Trump was also the subject of a fake quote that went viral. At the time, he was accused of referring to the President of Italy, Sergio Mattarella, as \"President Mozzarella.\" The claims began after a press conference was held between Trump and Mattarella. After the press conference, many claimed Trump mispronounced Mattarella's name and instead said \"President Mozzarella,\" but according to Snopes, there was no evidence showing this mispronunciation. {\"headline\":\"That Viral Lindsey Graham Quote Saying Trump Knows More About Viruses Than Scientists Is Fake\",\"datePublished\":\"2020-03-02T19:47:59.000Z\",\"dateModified\":\"2020-03-02T20:31:26.000Z\",\"author\":[{\"name\":\"Matthew Impelli\",\"jobTitle\":\"Life & Trends Reporter\"}],\"publisher\":{\"name\":\"Newsweek\",\"foundingDate\":\"1933-02-17\",\"sameAs\":[\"https://www.linkedin.com/company/newsweek\",\"https://www.facebook.com/Newsweek/\",\"https://twitter.com/newsweek\",\"https://www.instagram.com/newsweek/\",\"https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC2a35q7eyzkfoIusBzdH4Hw\",\"https://www.tiktok.com/@newsweek\",\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Newsweek\"],\"brand\":{\"name\":\"Newsweek\"},\"address\":{\"streetAddress\":\"1 World Trade Center, Floor 72\",\"addressLocality\":\"New York\",\"addressRegion\":\"NY\",\"postalCode\":\"10007\",\"addressCountry\":{\"name\":\"US\"}},\"founder\":{\"name\":\"Thomas J. C. Martyn\",\"jobTitle\":\"Newsweek Founder\"},\"contactPoint\":[{\"contactType\":\"Newsroom Contact\",\"email\":\"support@newsweek.com\"},{\"contactType\":\"Public Engagement\",\"email\":\"support@newsweek.com\"},{\"contactType\":\"Report corrections\",\"email\":\"support@newsweek.com\"},{\"contactType\":\"Customer support\",\"telephone\":\"+1-646-867-7100\"}]},\"inLanguage\":\"en\",\"alternativeHeadline\":\"Viral Lindsey Graham Quote Determined To Be Fake\",\"isAccessibleForFree\":false,\"hasPart\":{\"isAccessibleForFree\":false},\"articleSection\":\"News\",\"keywords\":[\"Lindsey Graham\",\"Donald Trump\",\"Twitter\"]}","title":"That Viral Lindsey Graham Quote Saying Trump Knows More About Viruses Than Scientists Is Fake - Newsweek","url":"https://www.newsweek.com/that-viral-lindsey-graham-quote-saying-trump-knows-more-about-viruses-scientists-fake-1490087"},{"position":5,"site_name":"m.fark.com","snippet":"- (Twitter)   Doctors feared Trump had an enlarged prostate. Turns out it was just Lindsey Graham 78 » Dan Lyons on Twitter \"CAPITOL HILL: @LindseyGrahamSC says @realDonaldTrump \"probably knows more about medicine and specifically viruses than any of the so-called scientists at the NIH and CDC. If anyone is going to eradicate this plague it'll be the president.\"\" 1999 Clicks 1999 Share Share on Twitter Twitter Share on Facebook Facebook Embed Link close » -   Original \\[TotalFark\\]   11 hours ago   Original Tweet: **realdanlyons**: CAPITOL HILL: @LindseyGrahamSC says @realDonaldTrump \"probably knows more about medicine and specifically viruses than any of the so-called scientists at the NIH and CDC. If anyone is going to eradicate this plague it'll be the president.\" https://t.co/lvQmrBtlwM Reply Share Share on Twitter Twitter Share on Facebook Facebook close -   ecmoRandomNumbers \\[TotalFark\\]   11 hours ago   \"...probably knows more about medicine and specifically viruses...\" Being Patient 0 of a herpes outbreak and a paradoxically obese amphetamine addict doesn't make one an expert in virology or pharmacology, Blanche. Smartest (36)   Funniest (15)   Reply Share Share on Twitter Twitter Share on Facebook Facebook close That was quoted \"specifically viruses than any of the so-called scientists at the NIH and CDC. If anyone is going to eradicate this plague it'll be the president.\"","title":"FARK.com: (10729129) Doctors feared Trump had an enlarged prostate. Turns out it was just Lindsey Graham","url":"https://m.fark.com/comments/10729129?from_page=politics"},{"position":6,"site_name":"www.trendsmap.com","snippet":"@realDonaldTrump CAPITOL HILL: @LindseyGrahamSC says Trump \"probably knows more about medicine and specifically viruses than any of the so-called scientists at the NIH and CDC. If anyone is going to eradicate this plague it'll be the president.\" ? https://t.co/NWUjvC3djD ### Replies and Quotes\nTotal of 95 replies and 9 quotes found\n\nAll Replies Quotes Retweeters\n\n```\n\tMEDIA_TYPE=''\n\ttrue\tfalse\t      \n```\n\nOG🚫💰2🐦↙️\n\n@K_OG_exGOP\n\n@LeeHolly81 @realDonaldTrump @LindseyGrahamSC That's quite possibly true. https://t.co/vq98kDcqaX\n\n· View on Twitter\n\n```\n\tMEDIA_TYPE=''\n\ttrue\tfalse\t      \n```\n\nDougDavid\n\n@DougDavid14 @LeeHolly81 @realDonaldTrump @LindseyGrahamSC Well, @LindseyGrahamSC has said some pretty darn stupid things but this may be at the top. \"So-called scientists?\" You mean those MDs and PhDs? Or is it \"so-called\" just because it's science and the Trump administration has demonstrated a disbelieve in science. Which is crazy.\n\n· View on Twitter\n\n```\n\tMEDIA_TYPE=''\n\ttrue\tfalse\t      \n```\n\nLoretta Mossman\n\n@Lorettm @LeeHolly81 @realDonaldTrump @LindseyGrahamSC Medical expert Trump is the first to say, \"It's only a cold sore.\" I won't add the other famous lies that go along with this one.\n\n· View on Twitter\n\n```\n\tMEDIA_TYPE=''\n