e thing is that he likes to kiss Trump’s a$$ & the other is to be that stupid thinking his boss knows better than the scientists!\n\n· View on Twitter\n\n```\n\tMEDIA_TYPE=''\n\ttrue\tfalse\t      \n```\n\nThis is fine!\n\n@chuckdubdubdub\n\n@LeeHolly81 @realDonaldTrump @LindseyGrahamSC Oy. You know he's owned.\n\n· View on Twitter ```\n\tMEDIA_TYPE=''\n\ttrue\tfalse\t      \n```\n\nDeana\n\n@Deana06119944\n\n@LeeHolly81 @realDonaldTrump @LindseyGrahamSC He doesn't understand how an umbrella works. Where did he do his post-grad work in microbiology and virology? https://t.co/wh12brohSf\n\n· View on Twitter\n\n```\n\tMEDIA_TYPE=''\n\ttrue\tfalse\t      \n```\n\n?Ashiya?\n\n@pbfa @Xtinaresists\n\n@LeeHolly81 @realDonaldTrump @LindseyGrahamSC Seriously how does Lindsey Graham day this crap woth a straight face. Has he lost his mind?\n\n· View on Twitter\n\n```\n\tMEDIA_TYPE=''\n\ttrue\tfalse\t      \n```\n\nTina'sTosaLife\n\n@dwellings_photo\n\n@LeeHolly81 @realDonaldTrump @LindseyGrahamSC Is @LindseyGrahamSC really that dumb ? No, seriously...is he? https://t.co/XUZYupwfm9 @LeeHolly81 @realDonaldTrump @LindseyGrahamSC Lindsay Graham know more about BS than anyone on the planet. If he ever contracts Corona he'll find out how knowledgeable the ? blob really is\n\n· View on Twitter\n\n```\n\tMEDIA_TYPE=''\n\ttrue\tfalse\t      \n```\n\n¯\\_(ツ)_/¯ 💙 OFFICIAL\n\n@EllisLauraLee\n\n@LeeHolly81 @realDonaldTrump @LindseyGrahamSC Hi Lindsey! America is hoping that you, #DonTheCon and the entire GOP are eradicated.\n\n· View on Twitter @LeeHolly81 @realDonaldTrump @LindseyGrahamSC It's not humanly possible to grovel more than Lindsey Graham.\n\n· View on Twitter\n\n```\n\tMEDIA_TYPE=''\n\ttrue\tfalse\t      \n```\n\nYea I said it\n\n@YeahIsa21707928\n\n@LeeHolly81 @realDonaldTrump @LindseyGrahamSC Did he really say this??\n\n· View on Twitter\n\n```\n\tMEDIA_TYPE=''\n\ttrue\tfalse\t      \n```\n\nAtheist Life\n\n@atheistyolo @LeeHolly81 @realDonaldTrump @LindseyGrahamSC Consider the source\n\n· View on Twitter\n\n```\n\tMEDIA_TYPE=''\n\ttrue\tfalse\t      \n```\n\nMaxblack\n\n@Maxblac41912419\n\n@LeeHolly81 @realDonaldTrump @LindseyGrahamSC The only thing in Graham's mouth,,is O very SMALL piece of trump\n\n· View on Twitter\n\n```\n\tMEDIA_TYPE=''\n\ttrue\tfalse\t      \n```\n\nSteph\n\n@Stefferz__ Lucy Ferres\n\n@LucyFerres\n\n@LeeHolly81 @realDonaldTrump @LindseyGrahamSC Yuck\n\n· View on Twitter\n\n```\n\tMEDIA_TYPE=''\n\ttrue\tfalse\t      \n```\n\nJanice Sullivan\n\n@Sullivan_J_A\n\n@LeeHolly81 @realDonaldTrump @LindseyGrahamSC What the hell is wrong with @LindseyGrahamSC? What does @realDonaldTrump have on him? It must be something very damaging for Graham to be whistling this tune.\n\n· View on Twitter @LeeHolly81 @realDonaldTrump @LindseyGrahamSC I believe that was from a parody account. Please let's not spread it around. What they are actually doing and saying is alarming enough without adding to it.\n\n· View on Twitter\n\n```\n\tMEDIA_TYPE=''\n\ttrue\tfalse\t      \n```\n\nKathleen Havig\n\n@kathleenshopper\n\nIsn’t this absolutely pathetic? Lindsey is obviously suffering from the same mental decline as Trump. https://t.co/isTLm4J5fB\n\n· View on Twitter ```\n\tMEDIA_TYPE=''\n\ttrue\tfalse\t      \n```\n\nKathy Merry 🇺🇸🌻\n\n@KathyMerry2\n\n@LeeHolly81 @realDonaldTrump @LindseyGrahamSC This is FAKE\n\n· View on Twitter\n\n```\n\tMEDIA_TYPE=''\n\ttrue\tfalse\t      \n```\n\nYou don’t know me\n\n@youdontknowdrek\n\n@LeeHolly81 @realDonaldTrump @LindseyGrahamSC Check Trumps safe....There are orgy tapes or other damning evidence in there somewhere. Linsey is scared. ```\n\tMEDIA_TYPE=''\n\ttrue\tfalse\t      \n```\n\nKathleen Caffey\n\n@caffey_kathleen\n\n@LeeHolly81 @realDonaldTrump @LindseyGrahamSC Lindsey is talking out of the wrong side of his body. Trump could not even begin to understand anything about any virus.\n\n· View on Twitter\n\n```\n\tMEDIA_TYPE=''\n\ttrue\tfalse\t      \n```\n\nHeat McD\n\n@Heat66195600\n\n@LeeHolly81 @realDonaldTrump @LindseyGrahamSC He can't even figure out umbrellas","title":"Holly Lee's tweet - \"@realDonaldTrump CAPITOL HILL: @LindseyGrahamSC says Trump \"probably knows more about medicine and specifically viruses than any of the so-called scientists at the NIH and CDC. If anyone is going to eradicate this plague it'll be the president.\" ? \" - Trendsmap","url":"https://www.trendsmap.com/twitter/tweet/1234469320731832322"},{"position":7,"site_name":"www.newsweek.com","snippet":"The South Carolina senator said he did not know what Trump was talking about after the president said the mortality rate for the novel coronavirus is under one percent. # Lindsey Graham Urges Donald Trump to ‘Make Sure Science Is Behind What He Says’ About Coronavirus\nLindsey Graham\n\nSenator Lindsey Graham urged President Donald Trump Thursday to \"make sure the science is behind what he says\" with regards to the new coronavirus. \"I would encourage the president if he's going to report things to make sure the science is behind what he says,\" Graham told CNN's senior congressional correspondent Manu Raju when asked about Trump saying he had a \"hunch\" that the death rate for the new disease, officially known as COVID-19, is under one percent. \"I don't know what he was talking about, but I listen to the scientists when it comes to the numbers.\" \"I think the 3.4% percent is really a false number. This is just my hunch, but based on a lot of conversations with a lot of people that do this. A lot of people will have [COVID-19] and it is very mild...they don't even call a doctor. You never hear about those people so you can't put them down in the category, the overall population in terms of this corona flu, or virus.\" the president told show host Sean Hannity. *Newsweek* reached out to U.S. health officials to ask if they concur with the president's comments. Dr. Brett P. Giroir, Assistant Secretary for Health and admiral in the U.S. Public Health Service Commissioned Corps, responded in an email Saturday. \"The best estimates from the CDC, with which I concur, are that the overall mortality rate is between 0.1% and 1%. That is the range based on data we have, and consistent with data from countries like Korea that have instituted widespread testing. The mortality in elderly or those with chronic health conditions is substantially higher and needs to be taken with the utmost seriousness.\" #### Read More\nThe Centers for Disease Control and Prevention website says there have been a total of 149 confirmed cases of COVID-19 in the U.S.. That total includes 49 cases among Americans repatriated to the United States from Wuhan, China, the epicenter of the novel coronavirus, and the Diamond Princess Cruise ship, which was quarantined of the coast of Japan for two weeks. Eleven people have died thus far in the U.S. as a result of the coronavirus.","title":"Lindsey Graham Urges Donald Trump to ‘Make Sure Science Is Behind What He Says’ About Coronavirus - Newsweek","url":"https://www.newsweek.com/lindsey-graham-urges-donald-trump-make-sure-science-behind-what-he-says-about-coronavirus-1490779"},{"position":8,"site_name":"www.independent.co.uk","snippet":"# Trump ally reprimands president for coronavirus comments and tells him to 'listen to the scientists'\n## Senator Lindsey Graham says that he would encourage the president 'to make sure the science is behind what he's saying'\nTrump ally reprimands president for coronavirus comments and tells him to 'listen to the scientists' Senator Lindsey Graham has sided with science over President Donald Trump's \"hunch\" contradicting the World Health Organisation's (WHO) coronavirus mortality rate figures.\n\n\"I listen to the scientists when it comes to the numbers, and I would encourage the president, if he's going to report things, to make sure the science is behind what he's saying.\" The president denied the official global death rate for coronavirus reported by health experts because he has a “hunch” it is lower. On Sunday, the WHO said that most patients (80 per cent) have experienced mild illness from coronavirus, while approximately 14 per cent experienced severe disease and 5 per cent became critically ill.\n\nHowever, those who have caught the virus are not recommended to go to work and have been told to self-isolate to prevent further spreading from the outbreaks. Congress is in the process of passing $8.3bn in emergency funding to counter the spread of the virus.\n\nThe latest reports indicate at least 160 cases have been confirmed in at least 17 states across the country. The death toll stands at 11.","title":"Trump ally reprimands president for coronavirus comments and tells him to 'listen to the scientists'","url":"https://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/americas/us-politics/trump-coronavirus-lindsey-graham-covid-19-cases-us-scientists-vaccine-twitter-a9378296.html"},{"position":9,"site_name":"www.businessinsider.com","snippet":"# GOP Sen. Lindsey Graham said Trump needs to 'make sure the science is behind' what he says on coronavirus\nU.S. President Donald Trump listens as Anthony Fauci, director of National Institute of Allergy and Infectious Diseases, and Health and Human Services (HHS) Secretary Alex Azar face reporters after they returned from a coronavirus briefing at the National Institutes of Health (NIH) Vaccine Research Center, on the South Lawn of the White House in Washington, U.S., March 3, 2020. - As President Donald Trump contines to share disinformation on coronavirus, Republican Sen. Lindsey Graham is urging the commander-in-chief to listen to the science.\n- \"I listen to the scientists when it comes to the numbers, and I would encourage the president if he's going to report things to make sure the science is behind what he's saying,\" Graham said Thursday. - This came after Trump told Fox News he had a \"hunch\" the death rate from the novel coronavirus was lower than what the World Health Organization has reported. Republican Sen. Lindsey Graham on Thursday encouraged President Donald Trump to ensure that the science is behind any statements he makes about it\n\n\"I listen to the scientists when it comes to the numbers, and I would encourage the president if he's going to report things to make sure the science is behind what he's saying,\" Graham, who is often one of Trump's fiercest defenders in Congress, told reporters. This came as Trump has shared a slew of disinformation on COVID-19, the disease caused by the virus, including during a Wednesday night interview with Sean Hannity on Fox News.\n\nDuring the Hannity interview, Trump challenged the World Health Organization's numbers on the death rate from coronavirus.\n\nThe global death rate for the novel coronavirus is 3.4%, according to the latest figures.","title":"GOP Sen. Lindsey Graham said Trump needs to 'make sure the science is behind' what he says on coronavirus","url":"https://www.businessinsider.com/lindsey-graham-trump-needs-to-listen-to-science-on-coronavirus-2020-3?r=US&IR=T"},{"position":10,"site_name":"talkingpointsmemo.com","snippet":"Sen. Lindsey Graham (R-SC) encouraged President Donald Trump to say things about a fatal respiratory virus that are actually based on science instead of a \"hunch.\" # Graham ‘Would Encourage’ Trump To Make Science-Based Coronavirus Comments\nSen. Lindsey Graham (R-SC) encouraged President Donald Trump to say things about a fatal respiratory virus that are actually based on science instead of a “hunch.”\n\nOn Thursday, reporters asked Graham for his response to Trump’s efforts to minimize the World Health Organization’s (WHO) estimated 3.4% death rate of reported COVID-19 cases worldwide. “I listen to the scientists when it comes to the numbers,” Graham said. “And I would encourage the President, if he’s going to report things, to make sure the science is behind what he’s saying.”\n\nTrump had appeared on Fox News host Sean Hannity’s program the night before, during which the President asserted that the 3.4% figure “is really a false number.” “Now this is just my hunch, but based on a lot of conversations with a lot of people that do this, because a lot of people will have this, and it’s very mild,” he told Hannity. “They’ll get better very rapidly, they don’t even see a doctor, they don’t even call a doctor, you never hear about those people.” > Graham says he \"would encourage\" Trump to make sure his comments about the coronavirus are backed up by science. pic.twitter.com/YoBOklJISd","title":"Graham 'Would Encourage' Trump To Make Science-Based Coronavirus Comments","url":"https://talkingpointsmemo.com/news/graham-would-encourage-trump-listen-scientists-coronavirus"}],"total_results":10,"page":0}